nodecode-handflow is a rewrite of DECRUX9812's DECRUX9812/hermes-handflow:

  https://github.com/DECRUX9812/hermes-handflow
  commit 6526ef75ffeb133d66472bc1899c87f34dcf9556
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Ritesh Patel (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plan store, the `handflow` tool with its twelve actions, the
plan rendering and the step vocabulary (not_started, in_progress, completed,
blocked, with a note on each step), the auto-complete of the open step when
another begins, the plan closing itself when its last step completes, and
reopening on an added or reopened step. The Python plugin kept one JSON file
per plan under the Hermes home; this cell keeps the same shape, one JSON file
per plan plus a pointer to the active one, written atomically, and the pane
and the tool read the same files.

Left out: the dockable desktop pane and its backend routes, which are Hermes
web UI with no Nodecode counterpart. What the pane gave the person, /handflow
now gives, and what it gave the model, a harness section carrying the active
plan in every request, now gives. The pane's one-click step toggles are
likewise read-only here: a step is moved by the tool or by the operator's
command, not by a click.
